---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PROJECTS } from '../data/projects.mjs';

const lifecycle = [
  ['Now playing', 'What the player is handling right now.', 'Temporary; it may never enter history.'],
  ['Progress', 'Where playback or reading can resume.', 'Changes often during one session.'],
  ['Scrobble', 'What happened, and when.', 'Durable history; it must be correctable.'],
  ['Completion', 'Whether a work or chosen unit counts as finished.', 'The policy depends on the medium and source.']
];

const mediaGroups = [
  ['Listening', 'Keep elapsed time, duration, recording, release, episode or feed context.'],
  ['Watching', 'Keep work, release, season, episode and order context.'],
  ['Reading', 'Keep edition, volume, chapter, issue or page context.'],
  ['Playing', 'Keep session, platform, turn, score or completion context when it matters.']
];

const schema = [{
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'DefinedTermSet',
  '@id': 'https://scrobble.dev/#terms',
  name: 'Scrobbling terms',
  url: 'https://scrobble.dev/#definition',
  inLanguage: 'en',
  hasDefinedTerm: [
    { '@type': 'DefinedTerm', name: 'Scrobble', description: 'A durable record of what someone watched, read, heard or played, and when.', url: 'https://scrobble.dev/#definition' },
    { '@type': 'DefinedTerm', name: 'Now playing', description: 'A temporary statement about media being handled by a player now.', url: 'https://scrobble.dev/#lifecycle' }
  ]
}];
---
<BaseLayout schema={schema} markdown="/knowledge/concepts/scrobbling.md" modified="2026-08-11" status="stable">
  <section class="shell home-hero" id="definition" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">Scrobbling, in plain language</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">Your media history should outlast the app that recorded it.</h1>
      <p class="standfirst">A scrobble is a durable record of what you watched, read, heard or played, and when. Done well, you can inspect and correct the record, then carry it elsewhere.</p>
      <p>The player knows what is happening now. A useful history remembers what happened then, without losing the original time, progress or source.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button primary" href="/learn/scrobbling/">Show me how scrobbling works</a>
        <a class="button" href="/projects/">Compare tracking projects</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <aside class="hero-brief" aria-labelledby="brief-title">
      <p class="brief-label" id="brief-title">A scrobble, caught in the act</p>
      <dl>
        <div><dt>Moment</dt><dd><time datetime="19:42">19:42</time>, while a track is playing</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Progress</dt><dd>3:18 of 5:37, kept as time</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Source</dt><dd>the player that observed it</dd></div>
        <div><dt>History</dt><dd>one correctable play, even after a retry</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="definition-band" aria-labelledby="paths-title">
    <div class="shell article-grid">
      <p class="section-label">Where the trouble starts</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="paths-title">The playhead moves every second. History has to make sense tomorrow.</h2>
        <p>A playhead can move every second. History should enter once, and it should still make sense after an import, a correction or a new app. Most readers arrive with one of two questions.</p>
        <div class="path-list">
          <article><h3>I use trackers</h3><p>I want a clean history I can understand, correct and move.</p><a href="/learn/">Start with the field guide</a></article>
          <article><h3>I build trackers</h3><p>I need events that survive retries, synchronization and export without making duplicates.</p><a href="/build/">Read the implementation guide</a></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell section" id="lifecycle" aria-labelledby="lifecycle-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p class="section-label">The activity lifecycle</p>
      <h2 id="lifecycle-title">One media session can produce four different records.</h2>
      <p>The distinction matters when a track repeats, an import runs twice or a person fixes the wrong entry.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="measure-table" role="table" aria-label="Media activity lifecycle">
      <div class="measure-row measure-head" role="row"><span role="columnheader">Record</span><span role="columnheader">Meaning</span><span role="columnheader">Boundary</span></div>
      {lifecycle.map(([record, meaning, boundary]) => <div class="measure-row" role="row"><strong role="cell">{record}</strong><span role="cell">{meaning}</span><span role="cell">{boundary}</span></div>)}
    </div>
    <p><a href="/learn/lifecycle/">Read the lifecycle guide</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="measure-band" aria-labelledby="media-title">
    <div class="shell section">
      <div class="section-intro">
        <p class="section-label">Across media</p>
        <h2 id="media-title">A page is not a second. Keep the unit that explains what happened.</h2>
        <p>A percentage is handy on a progress bar. The original unit lets a person understand, resume and correct the record.</p>
      </div>
      <dl class="media-groups">
        {mediaGroups.map(([group, detail]) => <div><dt>{group}</dt><dd>{detail}</dd></div>)}
      </dl>
      <p>The <a href="/standard/">draft principles</a> carry that rule into timestamps, identity, provenance, retry, correction and export. They are published for testing and comment, not as an adopted industry standard.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="shell section" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
    <div class="section-intro">
      <p class="section-label">From diaries to self-hosted trackers</p>
      <h2 id="projects-title">{PROJECTS.length} projects. Start with the job you need done.</h2>
      <p>A project might listen to a player, offer a diary, synchronize another service or hold a self-hosted history. The catalogue compares what each source establishes and leaves the ranking to you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="project-actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="/projects/">Compare {PROJECTS.length} projects</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/Electric-Town/scrobble.dev/issues/new">Add or correct a project</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/dannyvfilms/Floppy/issues">Take a reproducible case to Floppy</a>
    </div>
    <p class="reference-note">Floppy and FloppyDesktop appear as working software in the same catalogue. They also provide a place to turn a reproducible tracking failure into a test or code change.</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
